	(text "+5V out fuse (F801): the fused 5 V supply for a sensor on J1 pin 4"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc68af82-cdd7-52aa-bf08-84c922ea64c3")
	)
	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nJ1 pin 4 gives an external 5 V sensor (for example the one on AIN1) up to 200 mA from the board 5 V rail.\nF801 is a resettable fuse: a short on the sensor wire heats it and it cuts the current (trips above 0.46 A, in 0.1-0.4 s).\nIt cools down and conducts again by itself once the short is gone. The ESP32 may reset during the short.\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\n+5V (in): the board 5 V rail (5V buck module, or USB through the ESP32 + USB module)\nSENSOR_5V (out): to J1 pin 4: +5 V out, 4.8-4.9 V, 200 mA. Never connect it to the vehicle supply (5.5 V absolute maximum)\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 265 22.45)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "07e9aeab-1dfa-5194-b95c-bf15091e7a71")
	)
	(text "from the board 5 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 109.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6894eec8-621a-59eb-b297-54d6325c2b86")
	)
	(text "to J1 pin 4 (+5 V out)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 147.32 109.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "36137246-71e3-5cee-a2bd-ba3587a71b10")
	)
	(text "F801's place on the PCB is not critical: anywhere on the path from +5V to\nJ1 pin 4 it protects the sensor wire. (The routed board has it right behind J1.)\nTracks to and from F801: 0.5 mm or wider (Power class)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.76 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "08a8e3b9-4808-5704-a697-d673e6bcb3d5")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nF801: 0.2 A resettable fuse (PTC, 1206, SMD1206P020TF): carries 200 mA, trips above 0.46 A, resets itself when it cools. Protects the board 5 V rail from a short on the sensor wire at J1 pin 4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 156 0)
		(size 155 10.15)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
